{"model":"gpt-6-luna","messages":[{"role":"user","content":"Summarize the content of following sequence of messages for further reference:"},{"role":"user","content":"Help me get better sales results.","name":"student"},{"role":"assistant","content":"Improve results by leading with a tailored insight that reframes the buyer\u2019s problem, quantifying the cost of the status quo, then confidently guiding them to one clear next step.","name":"expert"},{"role":"user","content":"What should I do next?","name":"student"},{"role":"assistant","content":"Pick one target building LLM features, quantify the time and failure cost of unreliable outputs, then send a brief, tailored note showing how Instructor for PHP can return validated data and ask for a 15-minute workflow review.","name":"expert"},{"role":"user","content":"Give me one more actionable tip.","name":"student"},{"role":"assistant","content":"Before your next demo, ask prospects to show you one recent LLM output that broke their workflow, then quantify the rework it caused.","name":"expert"},{"role":"user","content":"How could I apply this in practice?","name":"student"},{"role":"assistant","content":"In your next call, ask a prospect to share a recent malformed LLM response, trace the rework it caused, then demo how Instructor for PHP validates and retries that exact case.","name":"expert"},{"role":"user","content":"Instructor for PHP is a framework-agnostic PHP library for extracting validated, structured data from LLM outputs. It supports text, chat, and image inputs; class-based or dynamic schemas; automatic validation and retry feedback; streaming; embeddings and context caching; and observability. A unified API works with providers including OpenAI, Anthropic, Google, Cohere, Groq, Mistral, and Ollama.\n\nTypical use: install with `composer require cognesy\/instructor-php`, define a PHP response class, then pass it and a prompt to `StructuredOutput` to receive a typed result. The library also supports Symfony validation and custom prompts, validation, and deserialization. It is intended for applications such as document processing, support automation, and analysis across industries, with extensive documentation and examples."}],"max_completion_tokens":512}